Modulo 2: X^5-X-1 = (X^2+X+1)(X^3+X^2+1).
Both factors are irreducible (degrees 2 and 3, with no roots), and distinct.
Modulo 3: no monic divisor of degree 1 or 2 (12 divisions checked).
A reducible degree-5 polynomial has a factor of degree at most 2, so it is irreducible.
Exact derived-subgroup orders: 120 60 60
Thus S5 is not solvable; its splitting field is not contained in Q^solv.
